You can refer to the same variable twice in the syntax, with differnt modifiers:
common =~ NA*FINC1 +x*FINC1 + x*FINC2 +
The set the variance of the factor to 1 either by using the "std.lv <http://std.lv>=T" option within the sem() function, or else explicitly setting the variance of common to 1 with
common~~1*common

