FIML is still not available for MSEM, but you can use multiple imputation (e.g., using the mice package in R, or the Blimp software outside of R). When you have saved each imputed data set as a list of data.frames, then you can pass it as the data= argument of runMI() in the semTools package. Some features for MSEM (e.g., fitted() and resid(), and therefore the SRMR values from fitMeasures()) will only be available in the development version:
