>
> Is there another way do get these residuals?

You can use the estimates to calculate predicted values manually.  It is tedious, but not difficult.  SEM estimates are just a bunch of regression equations.

Jarrett Byrnes (whose tutorial you refer to) wrote some functions  <https://github.com/simsem/semTools/pull/25/files>to do return casewise residuals and predicted values in the case of path analyses with observed variables.  I'm sure he would be willing to share them with you.

